@page
@model FaqModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Frequently asked questions";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Answers about MatchPredictor update times, confidence scores, empty cards, selection lists, ads, cookies, and responsible use.";
}

<div class="mp-container mp-legal">
    <div class="mp-page-header">
        <div>
            <p class="mp-page-kicker">Help</p>
            <div class="mp-page-title">
                <h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mp-legal-meta">
        Still stuck? <a href="/contact">Contact us</a> or email
        <a href="mailto:hello@matchpredictor.dev">hello@matchpredictor.dev</a>.
    </p>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>What does MatchPredictor publish?</h2>
        <p>
            A daily card of football picks across BTTS, Over 2.5, Under 2.5, Straight Win, and Draw,
            plus curated selection lists and a public settled-results record. See
            <a href="/about">About</a> and <a href="/methodology">Methodology</a> for detail.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>How often is the card updated?</h2>
        <p>
            Predictions are generated and refreshed on a twice-daily schedule in West Africa Time
            (including morning and early-afternoon runs). Selection lists typically appear after the
            5:00 AM or 1:00 PM WAT generation windows. Live scores update during the day as matches
            progress and finish.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>What does “confidence” mean?</h2>
        <p>
            Confidence is a calibrated probability estimate for the published outcome — not a tipster
            star rating. A higher number means the model is more certain after blending bookmaker
            prices, statistical models, and calibration. It does not mean the pick is guaranteed.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>Why are some days empty?</h2>
        <p>
            Picks only appear when they clear a market-specific publish threshold. Quiet fixture lists,
            missing market quotes (especially for BTTS), or temporary data gaps can produce a thin or
            empty card for a market. Empty states are intentional — we prefer silence over padding the
            page with low-quality picks.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>Where can I see past performance?</h2>
        <p>
            Open <a href="/results">Results</a> for recent settled published picks, including losses.
            The Betslips page also keeps a calendar of historical selection-list records.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>What are selection lists / betslips?</h2>
        <p>
            They are curated multi-leg combinations built from the day’s analysed card (for example
            Banker, Rollover, and Ladder styles). They are informational tools — optional export to a
            third-party sportsbook is available where configured, and is governed by that sportsbook’s
            own terms.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>Do you guarantee wins?</h2>
        <p>
            No. Football outcomes are uncertain. Past hit rate does not predict future results.
            MatchPredictor is an informational statistics product, not financial advice and not a
            bookmaker.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>Is the site for adults only?</h2>
        <p>
            Yes. The site is intended for users aged <strong>18 and over</strong>. See
            <a href="/Privacy#responsible-use">responsible use</a> and our
            <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>Do I need an account?</h2>
        <p>
            No. There are no public user accounts. Cart selections stay in your browser’s local storage
            until you clear them. Optional AI Chat may require an operator password when that feature
            is gated.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>How do ads and cookies work?</h2>
        <p>
            We serve non-personalized Google AdSense ads. Analytics and advertising cookies stay denied
            until you accept the cookie banner. Declining keeps first-party analytics and ad storage
            off. Full detail is in the <a href="/Privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>Why doesn’t every fixture appear?</h2>
        <p>
            Coverage follows the fixtures available in the daily input feeds and the markets we
            support. Unsupported specials (for example bookings-only fixtures) are filtered out.
            Threshold gating further reduces the list to picks the model is willing to publish.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>How can I get help or report a score error?</h2>
        <p>
            Email <a href="mailto:hello@matchpredictor.dev">hello@matchpredictor.dev</a> with the
            fixture, market, and what looks wrong. Use the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page for
            other topics (privacy, press, or general feedback).
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
